00:27:22.870 --> 00:27:27.470
And Mike Schur actually said that the gifts were incredibly hard to manage.

697
00:27:27.930 --> 00:27:30.110
Because they start off as Secret Santa.

698
00:27:30.110 --> 00:27:33.210
So, everybody had a person that they bought a specific gift for.

699
00:27:33.410 --> 00:27:37.550
And then you had to track the gifts as they went around in the Yankee swap.

700
00:27:37.810 --> 00:27:45.030
He actually, in the script of this episode, there is a whole page where he lists the gifts.

701
00:27:45.350 --> 00:27:46.810
Who bought who what?

702
00:27:46.810 --> 00:27:50.490
And he did this for Veda, our script supervisor.

703
00:27:50.830 --> 00:27:57.070
We haven't really talked about her, but Veda's job is to sit and watch every take that is filmed

704
00:27:57.070 --> 00:28:01.090
and make notes about everything that happens continuity-wise.

705
00:28:01.490 --> 00:28:03.430
So, I mean, like, really specific.

706
00:28:03.730 --> 00:28:09.790
So, like, if in a scene you take a drink of your tea on a certain line and then scratch your nose on

707
00:28:09.790 --> 00:28:14.910
another one, Veda writes it down so that you do it the same every time for editing purposes.

708
00:28:15.250 --> 00:28:15.390
Yeah.

709
00:28:15.650 --> 00:28:21.810
Veda would come up to us and say, Angela, you were holding that pen in your left hand in the first take.

710
00:28:22.030 --> 00:28:24.770
And in the second take, you picked it up and held it in your right hand.

711
00:28:25.210 --> 00:28:26.450
So, that's not going to match.

712
00:28:26.590 --> 00:28:30.290
So, you need to pick which hand you're going to hold that pen in and do it in every take the same way.

713
00:28:30.290 --> 00:28:35.150
Yeah, because otherwise, when you edit it together, the pen is magically bouncing from hand to hand.

714
00:28:35.910 --> 00:28:40.910
So, Mike was really worried about Veda in this episode.

715
00:28:41.310 --> 00:28:44.390
And so, he made this list just for Veda.

716
00:28:44.530 --> 00:28:46.130
And I have it from the script.

717
00:28:46.350 --> 00:28:47.350
Oh, fantastic.

718
00:28:47.490 --> 00:28:51.650
Okay, so this is what everyone was intended to give.

