01:11:32.980 --> 01:11:33.980
He's getting ready to leave.

1766
01:11:34.140 --> 01:11:34.960
He's going to go downstairs.

1767
01:11:36.340 --> 01:11:45.820
Meredith just walks into his office, takes off her top, and then Steve, as Michael, takes

1768
01:11:45.820 --> 01:11:47.480
a picture and then walks out.

1769
01:11:47.660 --> 01:11:48.960
I have a fan question.

1770
01:11:49.240 --> 01:11:53.440
Well, first of all, Kate, I really wanted Kate to be able to call in for this one.

1771
01:11:53.560 --> 01:11:57.500
I traded texts with her, but she is starting a tour with Dancing with the Stars.

1772
01:11:57.700 --> 01:11:58.120
Oh, yeah!

1773
01:11:58.200 --> 01:11:59.200
And she's traveling today.

1774
01:11:59.200 --> 01:12:03.140
She's on a plane, and she called me night before last, and she was like, Ange, I'm so

1775
01:12:03.140 --> 01:12:04.200
sorry I can't come in.

1776
01:12:04.340 --> 01:12:08.820
But she was like, I really do want to come in and talk about all things Meredith.

1777
01:12:09.080 --> 01:12:10.320
So she will come eventually.

1778
01:12:10.640 --> 01:12:11.340
Oh, that's good.

1779
01:12:11.340 --> 01:12:14.680
I have a feeling you might know the answer to this fan question.

1780
01:12:14.900 --> 01:12:15.080
Okay.

1781
01:12:15.800 --> 01:12:21.420
Carrie Schaub said, or maybe it's Carrie Shabe, said, when characters flash each other,

1782
01:12:21.620 --> 01:12:24.920
are the actors really flashing each other in real life?

1783
01:12:25.160 --> 01:12:26.180
No, no, no.

1784
01:12:26.320 --> 01:12:26.620
No.

1785
01:12:26.780 --> 01:12:27.080
No.

1786
01:12:27.320 --> 01:12:28.320
I mean, sort of.

1787
01:12:28.420 --> 01:12:28.660
Sort of.

1788
01:12:28.660 --> 01:12:28.960
But no.

1789
01:12:29.200 --> 01:12:31.040
I mean, it's still embarrassing.

1790
01:12:31.620 --> 01:12:36.560
Even if I had to, like, be in a bathing suit, I'd feel awkward.

1791
01:12:36.760 --> 01:12:37.200
You know what I mean?

1792
01:12:37.300 --> 01:12:38.580
Kate was wearing pasties.

1793
01:12:38.740 --> 01:12:39.480
Kate had things.

1794
01:12:39.480 --> 01:12:40.500
She was kind of covered.

1795
01:12:40.660 --> 01:12:42.520
Yeah, she had things over her hoo-hahs.

1796
01:12:42.680 --> 01:12:42.840
Yeah.

1797
01:12:43.100 --> 01:12:44.240
Steve is such a gentleman.

1798
01:12:44.420 --> 01:12:46.420
He said, Kate, I'm just going to look at, like, your neck.

1799
01:12:46.680 --> 01:12:47.000
Yeah.

1800
01:12:47.620 --> 01:12:48.840
Stare at your clavicle.

1801
01:12:49.060 --> 01:12:50.940
They had no crew inside.

1802
01:12:51.180 --> 01:12:51.300
Yep.

1803
01:12:51.420 --> 01:12:53.760
Her image wasn't on any monitors anywhere.

1804
01:12:54.100 --> 01:12:54.560
That's right.

1805
01:12:54.560 --> 01:12:57.160
And there was no chip in the digital camera.

1806
01:12:57.380 --> 01:12:58.940
So the flash goes off.

1807
01:12:59.020 --> 01:13:02.980
It looks like Michael's taking a picture, but there was actually never a picture taken.

1808
01:13:03.240 --> 01:13:03.620
Never a photo.

1809
01:13:03.800 --> 01:13:08.940
So they were very, very mindful of taking care of Kate in that moment.

1810
01:13:09.400 --> 01:13:13.460
Kate would go on as Meredith to take off her clothes.

1811
01:13:13.460 --> 01:13:14.520
Quite a bit.

1812
01:13:14.600 --> 01:13:15.060
Quite a bit.

1813
01:13:15.380 --> 01:13:20.780
One of my favorite things is that Kate's father wrote her a handwritten letter.

1814
01:13:21.000 --> 01:13:21.960
Oh, my goodness.

1815
01:13:22.380 --> 01:13:26.860
And all it said, this is her father, who, you know, Kate is from Pennsylvania.

1816
01:13:27.120 --> 01:13:32.480
And all it said was, dear Kate, stop taking your clothes off.

1817
01:13:32.720 --> 01:13:33.700
Love, Dad.

1818
01:13:33.960 --> 01:13:35.160
Oh, my gosh.

1819
01:13:36.280 --> 01:13:37.600
Oh, my gosh.

1820
01:13:38.460 --> 01:13:40.120
What did Kate do?

1821
01:13:40.260 --> 01:13:41.540
How did she respond to that?

1822
01:13:41.540 --> 01:13:42.780
She was like, oh, man.

1823
01:13:43.240 --> 01:13:45.700
Now, is that her dad having a sense of humor?

1824
01:13:45.700 --> 01:13:48.300
Or is that him being like, seriously, stop it?

1825
01:13:48.500 --> 01:13:49.220
I think both.

1826
01:13:49.400 --> 01:13:49.980
I think both.

1827
01:13:50.160 --> 01:13:50.460
All right.

1828
01:13:50.540 --> 01:13:52.120
Should we talk about the parking lot?

1829
01:13:52.320 --> 01:13:53.760
We're almost done here.

1830
01:13:54.300 --> 01:13:54.740
Yes.

1831
01:13:54.740 --> 01:13:56.060
Let's talk about the parking lot.

1832
01:13:56.200 --> 01:14:02.160
Because it is definitely one of the most magical moments that I remember in filming all nine years.

1833
01:14:02.160 --> 01:14:03.500
And we all say that.

1834
01:14:03.780 --> 01:14:04.000
Yeah.

1835
01:14:04.140 --> 01:14:07.560
People often ask, like, what were your favorite scenes?

1836
01:14:07.560 --> 01:14:14.340
And it's always hard to explain because sometimes your favorite scene, it doesn't seem like that exciting of a scene.

1837
01:14:14.480 --> 01:14:17.820
But it's what happened behind the scenes that make it your favorite.

1838
01:14:17.960 --> 01:14:19.720
And this parking lot scene is one of mine.

1839
01:14:20.340 --> 01:14:20.740
Definitely.

1840
01:14:21.160 --> 01:14:21.520
Definitely.

1841
01:14:22.000 --> 01:14:22.280
Okay.

1842
01:14:22.300 --> 01:14:23.940
So it's the end of the day.

1843
01:14:24.100 --> 01:14:26.320
We have all of this real snow on the ground.

1844
01:14:26.320 --> 01:14:28.220
And everyone is leaving.

1845
01:14:28.220 --> 01:14:29.860
And everyone's in good spirits.

1846
01:14:30.160 --> 01:14:31.360
And it's really nighttime.

1847
01:14:31.720 --> 01:14:34.100
It was rare for us to ever work past 6 p.m.

1848
01:14:34.120 --> 01:14:35.380
So we always got excited.

1849
01:14:35.660 --> 01:14:40.100
To walk out in the dark, I think, we all felt like we were up past our bedtime.

1850
01:14:40.360 --> 01:14:42.840
But also, you have to remember, this is Los Angeles.

1851
01:14:43.100 --> 01:14:44.960
There's never snow on the ground.

1852
01:14:45.120 --> 01:14:50.200
So this is magical in itself that we have a parking lot full of snow.

1853
01:14:50.700 --> 01:14:58.900
And as we're walking to the cars, I don't know, like, the shot you see, I'm actually in the front passenger seat of an SUV.

1854
01:14:59.120 --> 01:15:01.220
But I'm only half in, like, the door's open.

1855
01:15:01.480 --> 01:15:05.880
But I remember one of the guys just picked up some snow and flung it at the other one.

1856
01:15:06.120 --> 01:15:11.260
And then they all started picking up snow and having this impromptu snowball fight.

1857
01:15:11.360 --> 01:15:11.540
Yeah.

1858
01:15:11.760 --> 01:15:13.260
And everyone loved it.

1859
01:15:13.340 --> 01:15:14.840
And they wanted us to keep doing it.

1860
01:15:14.940 --> 01:15:19.600
But it was just sort of like us just all hanging out in the snow.

1861
01:15:19.600 --> 01:15:20.080
Yeah.

1862
01:15:20.480 --> 01:15:22.240
We turned into a bunch of kids.

1863
01:15:22.500 --> 01:15:22.860
We did.

1864
01:15:22.860 --> 01:15:23.500
We couldn't help it.

1865
01:15:23.600 --> 01:15:23.880
Yeah.

1866
01:15:24.040 --> 01:15:27.160
We were up past our bedtime with snow on the ground.

1867
01:15:27.580 --> 01:15:28.600
Fresh snow on the ground.

1868
01:15:28.980 --> 01:15:30.160
It was so fun.

1869
01:15:30.300 --> 01:15:37.000
And, you know, I have a picture of all of us together in the parking lot with Charles McDougal.

1870
01:15:37.460 --> 01:15:38.860
And it's great.

1871
01:15:39.080 --> 01:15:39.680
I love it.

1872
01:15:39.720 --> 01:15:40.580
I covet it.

1873
01:15:40.760 --> 01:15:41.700
I covet it.

1874
01:15:41.700 --> 01:15:41.840
I love that.

1875
01:15:41.920 --> 01:15:42.720
I want to see it.

1876
01:15:42.880 --> 01:15:43.160
Yeah.

1877
01:15:43.420 --> 01:15:46.780
Well, this is why we have to make our scrapbook thingy, Angela.

1878
01:15:47.020 --> 01:15:47.360
We do.

1879
01:15:48.400 --> 01:15:49.360
That's what we need to do.

1880
01:15:49.360 --> 01:15:52.740
We need to compile and combine all of our stuff.

1881
01:15:53.220 --> 01:15:56.400
And then make it so that we can both have what we both have.

1882
01:15:56.880 --> 01:15:57.280
Yeah.

1883
01:15:57.720 --> 01:15:58.080
Right?

1884
01:15:58.300 --> 01:15:58.600
Yeah.

1885
01:15:58.860 --> 01:15:59.080
Yeah.

1886
01:15:59.240 --> 01:16:01.480
Before we lose it all, we need to do it.

1887
01:16:02.080 --> 01:16:02.480
Okay.

1888
01:16:02.680 --> 01:16:03.480
It's 2020.

1889
01:16:04.760 --> 01:16:06.040
We need to do this.

1890
01:16:06.120 --> 01:16:07.240
This is a goal for this year.

1891
01:16:07.320 --> 01:16:09.080
I'm setting the goal for us this year.

1892
01:16:09.220 --> 01:16:10.840
Well, you guys, she said it.

1893
01:16:11.020 --> 01:16:13.940
Now I've got to, like, Jenna's going to put me to task.

1894
01:16:14.120 --> 01:16:15.600
This episode was really special.

1895
01:16:15.680 --> 01:16:16.120
It was.

1896
01:16:16.120 --> 01:16:19.760
I really hope we did it justice because it means so much to us.

1897
01:16:20.000 --> 01:16:25.040
These episodes are almost harder for me than other ones because there's so much emotion

1898
01:16:25.040 --> 01:16:25.880
attached to it.

1899
01:16:26.000 --> 01:16:27.840
There's so much that happens in the scene.

1900
01:16:28.300 --> 01:16:33.240
Not only, like, is it special to us personally, but it was, like, a big moment for our characters.

1901
01:16:33.520 --> 01:16:33.720
Yeah.

1902
01:16:33.720 --> 01:16:40.940
And just that moment at the end, that snowball fight, that is just a group of people who love

1903
01:16:40.940 --> 01:16:45.900
each other, who are all getting to hang out, and we just happen to be on a TV show together.

1904
01:16:46.140 --> 01:16:46.400
Yeah.

1905
01:16:46.400 --> 01:16:47.840
It's just a really special moment.

1906
01:16:47.840 --> 01:16:50.520
And I love that they let that be how it ended.

1907
01:16:50.800 --> 01:16:56.920
And that's really how it felt when we left this show, that we were just a bunch of friends who

1908
01:16:56.920 --> 01:17:01.580
happened to be on a TV show together because we were friends.

1909
01:17:01.860 --> 01:17:02.920
And we are friends.

1910
01:17:03.720 --> 01:17:04.460
And we're family.

1911
01:17:04.660 --> 01:17:05.120
We are.

1912
01:17:05.520 --> 01:17:08.960
So next week, we've got another big episode, Ange.

1913
01:17:09.200 --> 01:17:09.800
Huge episode.

1914
01:17:09.960 --> 01:17:17.300
I mean, listen, the rest of this season two is just going to be one momentous episode after

1915
